<title>GERMANY: BMW -growth forecast &quot;a misunderstanding&quot;.</title>
<headline>BMW -growth forecast &quot;a misunderstanding&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>German car group Bayerische Motoren Werke (BMW) said on Thursday that a growth forecast reportedly made by the company's chairman, Bernd Pischetsrieder, in Zurich on Wednesday was the result of a misunderstanding.</p>
<p>Reuters and other news agencies had reported that Pischetsrieder had responded to a question on expected 1997 profit developments with the response: &quot;There will certainly be slight growth.&quot;</p>
<p>Asked to be more specific, he replied: single digit growth.</p>
<p>BMW said on Thursday however that his comments referred to unit sales and not to profits, adding that the company generally refrained from making profit forecasts.</p>
<p>BMW shares had fallen in response to Wednesday's comments.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
